abstract: >-
  A settlement-level decision-support model for electrification planning. It
  clusters high-resolution building footprints into settlements using DBSCAN,
  estimates demand from household counts and standardised demand tiers, computes
  and compares the Levelized Cost of Electricity for grid extension, solar PV
  mini-grids and standalone solar PV, and evaluates financial viability by
  discounted cash flow from both utility and private-developer perspectives.
  Dispersed pastoralist homesteads, which most spatial models discard as
  clustering noise, are retained and tested explicitly.
